zy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rudolf Brun</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudolf Brun was the first burgomaster of Zürich.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-diesel"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rudolf-diesel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rudolf Diesel</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudolf Diesel was a German engineer who invented the diesel engine, a compression-ignition engine far more efficient than the steam engines of his day.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-duala-manga-bell"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rudolf-duala-manga-bell.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rudolf Duala Manga Bell</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudolf Duala Manga Bell was king of the Bell people of Douala in German Kamerun.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-burgundy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rudolf I of Burgundy</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudolf I, of the Welf family, was the first king of Upper Burgundy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rudolf I of Germany</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudolf I of Germany, a Swabian count of the Habsburg family, was elected King of the Romans in 1273, ending the Great Interregnum after the fall of the Hohenstaufen.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-duke-of-saxe-wittenberg"